{"_meta":{"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://comos/view-panel-v2-32905292888b.html","visibility":["model","app"]}},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Show One View of a Tenant"},"description":"Show one view of a tenant in the ComOS panel, filled from typed reads. Always pass tenant_id. Retail: product_grid (opt. category, in_stock_only), product_detail (product_id), order_status, receipt (order_id; owner). Bookings: slot_picker (opt. provider_id, from, to), provider_card (provider_id), booking_card (booking_id; owner). Digital: license_grid (opt. category), license_detail (license_id), entitlements (owner; opt. license_id, holder_ref). Services: capability_grid (opt. category), capability_detail (capability_id), job_status (job_id; owner). Rentals: asset_grid (opt. category, from, to), asset_detail (asset_id), rental_status (rental_id; owner). Buy, Book and each platform's act open ComOS pages; Details opens an item in place. Optional style: CSS on the drawn .c-<role> classes (see its parameter); the result names any selector that matched nothing. Public. Returns: { view, tenant_id, store_name, read_at, origin, ...payload } \u2014 also as structuredContent; the payload per view: products[] (product_grid), product (product_detail), providers[] + window + timezone (slot_picker), provider + next_slots[] + timezone (provider_card), booking (booking_card), order (order_status), order + lines[] + totals (receipt), capabilities[] (capability_grid), capability (capability_detail), job (job_status), assets[] + span? (asset_grid), asset (asset_detail), rental (rental_status). Refusals are isError: missing_argument, invalid_argument, not_a_storefront, storefront_disabled, not_a_booking_page, booking_page_disabled, calendar_unavailable, not_a_services_tenant, services_unavailable, not_a_rentals_tenant, rentals_unavailable, not_found, scope_required, or the inner tool's own refusal \u2014 each carrying `view`. E